1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,280
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:04,600
I'm Peppa Pig.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:05,680
[SNORTS]

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,279
This is my little brother,
George.

5
00:00:07,279 --> 00:00:08,240
[SNORTING]

6
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,480
This is Mummy Pig.

7
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:10,479
[SNORTS]

8
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:11,879
And this is Daddy Pig.

9
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,840
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGHING]

10
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:14,920
Peppa Pig.

11
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,760
[SNORTS]

12
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,599
[♪♪♪]

13
00:00:17,599 --> 00:00:19,360
PEPPA: Pen Pal.

14
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:21,720
NARRATOR: Peppa and her friends
are at playgroup.

15
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:25,640
Children,
who would like a pen pal?

16
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:26,640
ALL: Me!

17
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:27,639
Me!

18
00:00:27,639 --> 00:00:29,720
[SNORTS]
What's a pen pal?

19
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:34,559
A pen pal is a boy or girl
you can write letters to.

20
00:00:34,559 --> 00:00:37,600
This little girl lives
in France.

21
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,280
Her name is Delphine Donkey.

22
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:42,400
[SNORTS]
Can Delphine Donkey

23
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,440
be my pen pal?

24
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,199
Of course, Peppa.

25
00:00:45,199 --> 00:00:46,199
Hooray!

26
00:00:46,199 --> 00:00:47,519
[LAUGHS]

27
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:49,879
[HORN HONKING]

28
00:00:49,879 --> 00:00:51,400
NARRATOR:
It is early morning.

29
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:54,239
Mr. Zebra the Postman
is delivering a letter

30
00:00:54,239 --> 00:00:55,640
to Peppa's house.

31
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:56,839
Post!

32
00:00:56,839 --> 00:00:58,400
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George love it

33
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,400
when the post arrives.

34
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,959
[SNORTS]
It's addressed

35
00:01:00,959 --> 00:01:02,440
to "Miss Peppa Pig."

36
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:03,640
That's me.

37
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,119
[SNORTS]
Mummy,

38
00:01:05,119 --> 00:01:06,600
can you read it for me?

39
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,840
Of course.

40
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:10,240
It's from Delphine Donkey.

41
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:11,440
My pen pal!

42
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:13,000
[GIGGLES]

43
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
What does she say?

44
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,520
Bonjour, Peppa.

45
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,840
[SPEAKING IN FRENCH]

46
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:22,039
Mummy, why are you
saying those funny words?

47
00:01:22,039 --> 00:01:23,479
It's French, Peppa.

48
00:01:23,479 --> 00:01:26,119
It means,
"Hello, how are you?"

49
00:01:26,119 --> 00:01:27,600
What else does she say?

50
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:28,560
Hm.

51
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:29,640
I'll help.

52
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:35,679
[SPEAKING IN FRENCH]

53
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:37,759
Heh-heh-heh. Clever Daddy.

54
00:01:37,759 --> 00:01:40,479
[LAUGHS]
I am an expert in French.

55
00:01:40,479 --> 00:01:42,360
[SNORTS]
What does it mean?

56
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,199
Um...

57
00:01:44,199 --> 00:01:46,080
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig cleans his glasses,

58
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:48,440
so he can see
the letter more clearly.

59
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,880
Hm.

60
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,199
It's no good.

61
00:01:51,199 --> 00:01:52,839
It's nonsense.

62
00:01:52,839 --> 00:01:54,280
It means,

63
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,360
"I like fairy princesses

64
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:58,199
and playing
with my friends."

65
00:01:58,199 --> 00:01:59,960
That's what
I was going to say.

66
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,280
[ALL LAUGHING]

67
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:04,240
I want to talk French.

68
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,559
Maybe you could talk
to Delphine Donkey.

69
00:02:06,559 --> 00:02:07,720
How?

70
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:10,199
Her phone number
is on this letter.

71
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:11,359
Yippee!

72
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,920
[LAUGHING]

73
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,880
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

74
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,959
[SPEAKING FRENCH]

75
00:02:21,799 --> 00:02:25,160
NARRATOR: Mummy Pig is asking
if Peppa may speak to Delphine.

76
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,200
Hello?

77
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:27,440
Bonjour.

78
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,040
Bonjour.

79
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,320
Um...

80
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:32,359
[IN ENGLISH]
What do I say next?

81
00:02:32,359 --> 00:02:34,160
[SPEAKS IN FRENCH]

82
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,440
[SPEAKS IN FRENCH]

83
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:37,359
[LAUGHS]

84
00:02:37,359 --> 00:02:38,400
[IN ENGLISH]
Bye-bye.

85
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,359
[BOTH SPEAKING IN FRENCH]

86
00:02:41,359 --> 00:02:42,720
[IN ENGLISH]
What did she say?

87
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,560
She spoke French.

88
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:45,760
[CLEARS THROAT]

89
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,799
Bonjour, George.

90
00:02:47,799 --> 00:02:49,640
[SPEAKING IN FRENCH]

91
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,640
NARRATOR:
Peppa is saying
"How are you?" in French.

92
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:53,880
Dine-Saw.

93
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,000
[GROWLS]

94
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,440
No, George.

95
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:59,079
That's not how you speak
French.

96
00:02:59,079 --> 00:03:01,200
[BOTH LAUGHING]

97
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,720
[HORN HONKING]

98
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,320
NARRATOR:
It is morning.
Mr. Zebra the Postman

99
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,400
is delivering letters
to Peppa's house.

100
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,440
Post!

101
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:09,440
Hooray!

102
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,840
Can I have my letter

103
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,519
from Delphine, please?

104
00:03:12,519 --> 00:03:15,320
Sorry, Peppa,
there's no letter for you today.

105
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,840
Aw.
[DOORBELL RINGING]

106
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,880
I wonder who that could be.

107
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:22,239
Bonjour.
I am Delphine Donkey.

108
00:03:22,239 --> 00:03:23,320
[BRAYS]

109
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,840
I have come to see Peppa.

110
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,359
It's Delphine!

111
00:03:26,359 --> 00:03:27,519
Bonjour!

112
00:03:27,519 --> 00:03:28,480
[SNORTS]

113
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,519
Bonjour, Peppa.

114
00:03:29,519 --> 00:03:30,560
[BRAYS]

115
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,359
Here are my mama and papa

116
00:03:32,359 --> 00:03:33,799
and my brother, Didier.

117
00:03:33,799 --> 00:03:35,040
BOTH:
Bonjour.

118
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:36,000
[BOTH BRAY]

119
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,840
Here are my mommy and daddy

120
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,880
and my little brother,
George.

121
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,519
BOTH:
Hello.

122
00:03:41,519 --> 00:03:42,840
Dine-Saw.

123
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,920
[GROWLS]

124
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:45,040
Dragon.

125
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:46,079
[ROARS]

126
00:03:46,079 --> 00:03:47,160
[BOTH LAUGHING]

127
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,280
[BRAYS]

128
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,440
Do you speak French,
Mr. Pig?

129
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:52,920
[SNORTS]
I'm an expert at French.

130
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,959
[SPEAKING FRENCH]

131
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,920
Um...

132
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,000
Yes.

133
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,839
[ALL LAUGHING]

134
00:04:01,839 --> 00:04:07,040
Delphine, we could jump up
and down in muddy puddles.

135
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:10,119
NARRATOR: Delphine
does not understand Peppa.

136
00:04:10,119 --> 00:04:12,560
[SPEAKING FRENCH]

137
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:14,760
NARRATOR: Peppa does not
understand Delphine.

138
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:18,399
Everything's so different
in French, Daddy.

139
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:19,399
[BRAYS]

140
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:20,680
[IN ENGLISH]
Come on, Peppa.

141
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,640
[BOTH LAUGHING]

142
00:04:24,159 --> 00:04:26,840
[SPEAKING FRENCH]

143
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,120
Ah!

144
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,640
That's what I was going
to show you.

145
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:34,920
We call it jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

146
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,520
[LAUGHING]
[BRAYING]

147
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:40,479
J'adore jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

148
00:04:40,479 --> 00:04:42,240
NARRATOR:
Everyone in the whole world

149
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,560
loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

150
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,919
[SNORTING]
[BRAYING]

151
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:49,719
[♪♪♪]

152
00:04:49,719 --> 00:04:52,840
PEPPA:
Granny and Grandpa's Attic.

153
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,440
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George are playing

154
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,120
at Granny and Grandpa's house
today.

155
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,880
[SNORTS]
Hello, Grandpa Pig.

156
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:58,880
Papa Ig.

157
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,000
[CHUCKLES]

158
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,200
Hello, Peppa.

159
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,719
Hello, George.

160
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,039
[BOTH GIGGLING]
[SNORTS]

161
00:05:04,039 --> 00:05:06,039
Bye-bye. See you later.

162
00:05:06,039 --> 00:05:07,039
See you later.

163
00:05:07,039 --> 00:05:08,080
[SNORTING]

164
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,640
[ENGINE STARTS
THEN HORN HONKS]

165
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,800
Where's Granny Pig?

166
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,479
GRANNY:
Hello, my little ones.

167
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:15,400
NARRATOR:
That is Granny Pig's voice.

168
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,840
But where is she?

169
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,400
Granny Pig?

170
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,840
[SNORTS]
Here I am.

171
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,120
Granny Pig!

172
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,680
Gangy Ig!

173
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:25,240
Why is Granny in the roof?

174
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:27,159
We're tidying the attic.

175
00:05:27,159 --> 00:05:28,599
What's the attic?

176
00:05:28,599 --> 00:05:32,479
It's where we keep
all our old things.

177
00:05:32,479 --> 00:05:34,440
Like you, Grandpa Pig?

178
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,719
[LAUGHS]

179
00:05:35,719 --> 00:05:38,400
Things that are even older
than me.

180
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,359
[LAUGHS]

181
00:05:39,359 --> 00:05:40,479
Can we help?

182
00:05:40,479 --> 00:05:41,520
[SNORTS]
Okay.

183
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,880
[LAUGHING]

184
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:45,159
NARRATOR:
Granny and Grandpa's attic

185
00:05:45,159 --> 00:05:48,280
is at the very top
of the house.

186
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,200
That's the door
to the attic.

187
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:52,479
[SNORTS]
How do we get up there?

188
00:05:52,479 --> 00:05:55,359
I have a clever trick.

189
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,039
Hello, my little ones.

190
00:05:59,039 --> 00:06:00,240
It's Granny.

191
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,800
Come on up.

192
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,719
[CLANGING]

193
00:06:02,719 --> 00:06:04,120
BOTH:
Ooh.

194
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,520
[BOTH LAUGHING]

195
00:06:07,039 --> 00:06:08,400
This is our attic.

196
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,760
BOTH: Wow.

197
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,000
It's very full.

198
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,280
Yes, it's full of old junk.

199
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,680
[GRANDPA &amp; GRANNY
LAUGHING]

200
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,200
[SNORTS]
Peppa and George are here

201
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:19,120
to help us
throw some things out.

202
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:22,479
Good. Let's start
by throwing out this box.

203
00:06:22,479 --> 00:06:24,760
Oh! Not that box!

204
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:26,280
Do we really need this?

205
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:28,680
That's my ship in a bottle.

206
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,840
And this?

207
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:32,080
That's my other ship
in a bottle.

208
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,320
And these?

209
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:36,000
They're my other ships
in bottles.

210
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,760
I need them all.

211
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,120
[ALL LAUGHING]

212
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:41,719
Well, we have
to throw something out.

213
00:06:41,719 --> 00:06:44,080
Uh, how about this box?

214
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:46,680
No. Not my hats.

215
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:49,120
[BOTH LAUGHING]

216
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:54,240
Oh, dear, we can't decide
what to throw out.

217
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,400
I know.

218
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,240
We'll let Peppa
and George decide.

219
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:58,799
Okay. Heh-heh-heh.

220
00:06:58,799 --> 00:07:01,719
Let's throw away
this old case.

221
00:07:01,719 --> 00:07:04,520
BOTH:
Aah! Not that one!

222
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:07,320
This isn't
just any old case.

223
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,039
It's a record player.

224
00:07:09,039 --> 00:07:10,520
PEPPA &amp; GEORGE:
Ooh.

225
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:13,239
And this
was our favorite record.

226
00:07:13,239 --> 00:07:15,280
Can we play it?
Yes.

227
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,359
[LAUGHS]

228
00:07:16,359 --> 00:07:19,680
We haven't heard it
for years.

229
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:22,159
['50s ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:07:24,159 --> 00:07:25,640
[LAUGHS]

231
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,680
This takes me back.

232
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:29,000
[ALL LAUGHING]

233
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:33,479
Come on, Peppa and George,
let's dance.

234
00:07:33,479 --> 00:07:35,560
[ALL LAUGHING]

235
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,520
[RECORD CONTINUES PLAYING]

236
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:41,760
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig is here

237
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,440
to pick up
Peppa and George.

238
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,719
[DOORBELL RINGS]

239
00:07:45,719 --> 00:07:48,000
Hello?

240
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,359
Where are you?

241
00:07:49,359 --> 00:07:51,880
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig cannot find anyone.

242
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,400
What's that noise?

243
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:55,320
[ALL LAUGHING]

244
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:56,359
PEPPA &amp; GEORGE:
Mummy!

245
00:07:56,359 --> 00:07:57,560
Hello.

246
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:59,560
[SNORTS]
We've been dancing

247
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:02,200
to Granny and Grandpa's
favorite record.

248
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,520
Yes.

249
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:06,760
Granny and Grandpa played it
all the time.

250
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,960
Ooh.

251
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:10,000
And here's the record
I used to play

252
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,080
when I was a little piggy.

253
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:12,440
PEPPA:
What is it?

254
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:15,000
It's called
"Birdie Birdie Woof Woof."

255
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:19,760
Not "Birdie Birdie Woof Woof."
You were always playing that.

256
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:22,239
I thought we'd thrown that out
ages ago.

257
00:08:23,599 --> 00:08:26,200
[POP AND ZIP SOUND EFFECTS
PLAYING WITH MUSIC]

258
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,880
WOMAN: ♪ The birds go woof
And the dogs go tweet ♪

259
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:31,560
♪ Woof, tweet, woof, tweet
Woof, woof, woof ♪

260
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:34,439
♪ The sheep go moo
And the cows go baa ♪

261
00:08:34,439 --> 00:08:37,640
♪ Moo, baa, woof, tweet
Woof, baa, moo, tweet ♪

262
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:39,240
♪ Woof, woof, woof ♪

263
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,799
[ALL LAUGHING]

264
00:08:40,799 --> 00:08:42,159
Again, again!

265
00:08:42,159 --> 00:08:44,319
[POP AND ZIP SOUND EFFECTS
PLAYING WITH MUSIC]

266
00:08:45,199 --> 00:08:46,520
♪ The birds go woof ♪

267
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,800
♪ And the dogs go tweet ♪

268
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,560
♪ Woof, tweet
Woof, tweet ♪

269
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:50,720
♪ Woof, woof, woof ♪

270
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,079
♪ The sheep go moo ♪

271
00:08:52,079 --> 00:08:53,560
♪ And the cows go baa ♪

272
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:55,040
♪ Moo, baa, woof, tweet ♪

273
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,360
♪ Woof, baa, moo, tweet ♪

274
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,920
♪ Woof, woof, woof ♪♪

275
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:59,680
[ALL LAUGHING]

276
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,079
That was fun.

277
00:09:01,079 --> 00:09:03,199
But we were supposed
to be finding

278
00:09:03,199 --> 00:09:04,920
some things to throw out.

279
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:08,280
Peppa, what should we throw out
and what should we keep?

280
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,400
Hm.

281
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:12,560
I think you should
keep everything.

282
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:14,040
[ALL LAUGHING]

283
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:16,920
[♪♪♪]

284
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,520
[♪♪♪]

285
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,959
PEPPA:
The Quarrel.

286
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:30,040
NARRATOR:
Peppa and Suzy Sheep
are playing Snap.

287
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:32,920
Snap! I win.
[BOTH LAUGH]

288
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:35,520
NARRATOR: Peppa and Suzy
are best friends.

289
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:38,199
[BAAS]

290
00:09:38,199 --> 00:09:40,520
Snap! I win again.

291
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:41,560
[LAUGHING]

292
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:43,480
[SNORTS]
You cheated.

293
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,920
I did not.

294
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:46,800
You looked at the card.

295
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,439
I did not.

296
00:09:48,439 --> 00:09:50,520
[SNORTS]
I don't want to play

297
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,600
with you anymore.

298
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:52,920
[SNORTS]

299
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:54,920
I don't want
to play with you anymore.

300
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:55,839
[BLOWS RASPBERRY]

301
00:09:55,839 --> 00:09:57,160
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear.

302
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:59,000
Peppa and Suzy
have had a quarrel.

303
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,160
[DOORBELL RINGS]

304
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:02,040
NARRATOR:
Mummy Sheep is here,

305
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,360
to take Suzy home.

306
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,720
Peppa, say bye-bye to Suzy.

307
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:08,319
[SNORTS]
I am not talking to her.

308
00:10:08,319 --> 00:10:10,720
And I am not talking to her.

309
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:12,199
Oh. Ha, ha.

310
00:10:12,199 --> 00:10:13,760
I'm sure they'll make it up.

311
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,760
They are best friends
really.

312
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:17,240
It is not funny.

313
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,640
We are not best friends
anymore.

314
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:23,120
[♪♪♪]

315
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:25,640
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig is making supper.

316
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,800
Peppa! George!

317
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:29,000
Suppertime!

318
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,800
It's spaghetti!

319
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,839
[SNORTS AND CHUCKLES]

320
00:10:34,079 --> 00:10:36,120
[SLURPING AND MUNCHING]

321
00:10:37,079 --> 00:10:38,360
[SIGHS]

322
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,959
What's the matter, Peppa?

323
00:10:39,959 --> 00:10:42,600
Peppa and Suzy
have had a little quarrel.

324
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,680
Oh.

325
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:47,120
[SNORTS]
But I do miss Suzy a bit.

326
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,160
Hm.
Let's give Suzy a call.

327
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:51,560
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

328
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:53,120
[RINGING]

329
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,600
[BAAS]
Hello, Mrs. Pig.

330
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:59,000
[SNORTS]
May Peppa talk with Suzy please?

331
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,560
Hello, Suzy.

332
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,839
Hello, Peppa.

333
00:11:01,839 --> 00:11:05,040
We can be friends again,
if you say "sorry."

334
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:08,240
I'm sorry
I said you cheated.

335
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:10,920
Even though you did cheat.

336
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:15,719
Well, I'm sorry
you were ever my best friend.

337
00:11:15,719 --> 00:11:16,959
[DIAL TONE HUMS]

338
00:11:16,959 --> 00:11:18,120
Oh.

339
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,719
It doesn't matter.

340
00:11:19,719 --> 00:11:24,240
I can easily find
a new best friend.

341
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,079
NARRATOR:
It is a lovely sunny day.

342
00:11:26,079 --> 00:11:28,360
All the children
are at the playground.

343
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,319
Danny Dog
is on the roundabout,

344
00:11:30,319 --> 00:11:32,120
with his best friend,
Pedro Pony.

345
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,920
BOTH:
Whee!

346
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,400
NARRATOR:
George is on the seesaw,

347
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,640
with his best friend,
Richard Rabbit.

348
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:39,079
Seesaw.

349
00:11:39,079 --> 00:11:41,360
Seesaw.
[BOTH LAUGH]

350
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:45,240
NARRATOR: Suzy Sheep is
on the swings, on her own.

351
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,480
[SIGHS]

352
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:48,760
NARRATOR:
Peppa is playing mini golf,

353
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:50,400
on her own.

354
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:51,680
[SIGHS]

355
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,319
NARRATOR:
Here is Emily Elephant.

356
00:11:53,319 --> 00:11:54,560
Can I have a go?

357
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:55,560
Yes.

358
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,319
[LAUGHING]

359
00:11:57,319 --> 00:12:01,839
Emily, Suzy Sheep
is not my best friend anymore.

360
00:12:01,839 --> 00:12:04,839
[SNORTS]
So you can be my best friend.

361
00:12:04,839 --> 00:12:07,719
But my best friend
is Candy Cat.

362
00:12:07,719 --> 00:12:09,040
Oh.
[MEOWS]

363
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:11,120
[BOTH LAUGHING]

364
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,920
Whee!

365
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:17,520
Zoe, if you want,
you can be my best friend.

366
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:20,719
But my best friend
is Rebecca Rabbit.

367
00:12:20,719 --> 00:12:21,680
Oh.

368
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:22,760
Whee!

369
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:24,360
[BOTH LAUGHING]

370
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,240
PEPPA [SNORTS]:
Hello, Suzy.

371
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,760
Hello, Peppa.

372
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:29,000
Ah, good.

373
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,079
I see you two
are friends again.

374
00:12:31,079 --> 00:12:32,640
We are not friends.

375
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:34,959
We will never be friends
again.

376
00:12:34,959 --> 00:12:38,760
Hm. I think it's about time
you two made it up.

377
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:41,040
Peppa, say sorry to Suzy.

378
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:45,000
Only if she says sorry
first.

379
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,560
Only if she says sorry
first.

380
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,719
DADDY PIG:
I know.

381
00:12:48,719 --> 00:12:50,199
I'll count to three

382
00:12:50,199 --> 00:12:53,079
and you can both say sorry
at the same time.

383
00:12:53,079 --> 00:12:54,400
BOTH:
All right.

384
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:57,040
DADDY PIG:
One, two, three.

385
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:58,240
BOTH [IN UNISON]:
Sorry.

386
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:00,400
Now you can be
best friends again.

387
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,839
BOTH:
Hooray!

388
00:13:01,839 --> 00:13:02,880
[BOTH LAUGHING]

389
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:05,400
Suzy, let's play
mini golf.

390
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,880
Good idea.

391
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:09,360
NARRATOR:
Peppa and Suzy
are best friends again.

392
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:11,800
Me first.

393
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:14,480
My go.

394
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:17,760
My ball went in the hole,
so I win.

395
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:21,439
But my ball knocked it in,
so I win.

396
00:13:21,439 --> 00:13:23,839
You're just
making the rules up.

397
00:13:23,839 --> 00:13:25,920
You were
making the rules up.

398
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:27,079
I win!

399
00:13:27,079 --> 00:13:28,760
No, I win!

400
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:29,880
[DADDY PIG LAUGHS]

401
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:32,599
You two are just the same.

402
00:13:32,599 --> 00:13:33,800
[CHUCKLES]

403
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:35,959
That's why
Suzy is my best friend

404
00:13:35,959 --> 00:13:37,560
in the whole world.

405
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,719
[LAUGHS]

406
00:13:38,719 --> 00:13:41,640
And Peppa is my best friend

407
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,560
in the whole world, ever.

408
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:45,640
[ALL LAUGHING]

409
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:50,800
[♪♪♪]

410
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:53,520
PEPPA:
The Toy Cupboard.

411
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:55,680
NARRATOR: It is Peppa
and George's bedtime.

412
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:58,599
[BOTH LAUGHING]

413
00:13:58,599 --> 00:14:00,000
Goodness me.

414
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,880
Why are all these toys
on your bed?

415
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:04,280
[SNORTS]
That's where they live.

416
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:07,640
Quickly, put the toys away
in your toy basket.

417
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:09,839
But the toy basket is full.

418
00:14:09,839 --> 00:14:11,680
MUMMY PIG:
Oh, so it is.

419
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:14,160
Maybe you need
a toy cupboard.

420
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:17,319
Yes. I could make one tomorrow.
[SNORTS]

421
00:14:17,319 --> 00:14:19,599
The last thing you made,
Daddy Pig,

422
00:14:19,599 --> 00:14:20,680
was this shelf.

423
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,920
I am very proud
of that shelf.

424
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,439
But, Daddy, it's all wobbly.

425
00:14:25,439 --> 00:14:28,000
[SNORTS]
We use it as a slide.

426
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,160
For Teddy and Mr. Dinosaur.

427
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:32,120
[ALL LAUGHING]

428
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,920
All right, let's buy
a new toy cupboard.

429
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,599
We can buy one now,
on the computer.

430
00:14:37,599 --> 00:14:39,160
Hooray!
[SNORTING]

431
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,479
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig is using the computer

432
00:14:42,479 --> 00:14:43,719
to buy a toy cupboard.

433
00:14:43,719 --> 00:14:44,760
Ah-ha.

434
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,160
Now, which one shall we get?

435
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:49,439
Can we have this one, please?

436
00:14:49,439 --> 00:14:51,520
MUMMY PIG:
That looks perfect.

437
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:53,560
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig is buying
the toy cupboard.

438
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,839
[CASH REGISTER RINGS]

439
00:14:54,839 --> 00:14:56,120
FEMALE COMPUTER VOICE:
Congratulations.

440
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:58,520
Your toy cupboard
is ordered.

441
00:14:58,520 --> 00:14:59,680
Oh, goody.

442
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:01,079
[♪♪♪]

443
00:15:01,079 --> 00:15:02,719
[ROOSTER CROWS]

444
00:15:02,719 --> 00:15:05,520
NARRATOR: It is morning,
and Mr. Zebra the Postman

445
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:06,719
has a special delivery.

446
00:15:06,719 --> 00:15:08,800
[HORN HONKING]

447
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:09,800
Post!

448
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:11,479
[BOTH LAUGHING]

449
00:15:11,479 --> 00:15:12,959
Special delivery

450
00:15:12,959 --> 00:15:15,800
for Miss Peppa Pig
and Master George.

451
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:17,079
What is it?

452
00:15:17,079 --> 00:15:18,880
It's a toy cupboard.

453
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:22,199
Oh. It looks a bit flat.

454
00:15:22,199 --> 00:15:24,400
Yes. You build it yourself.

455
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:25,479
Oh.

456
00:15:25,479 --> 00:15:27,280
Don't worry, Peppa.

457
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:28,640
It'll be very easy

458
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:31,640
for your mommy and daddy
to build. Goodbye.

459
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:32,719
BOTH:
Bye-bye.

460
00:15:32,719 --> 00:15:35,120
Bye.

461
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,599
Now what do we do?

462
00:15:36,599 --> 00:15:38,880
Now we build
your toy cupboard.

463
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:39,880
Yes.

464
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,959
[BOTH LAUGH]

465
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:46,400
That's strange.

466
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,079
There aren't
any instructions.

467
00:15:48,079 --> 00:15:50,319
Maybe it's so easy to build

468
00:15:50,319 --> 00:15:52,599
it doesn't need
instructions.

469
00:15:52,599 --> 00:15:55,240
[SNORTS]
Mummy, can we help?

470
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,319
Yes.

471
00:15:56,319 --> 00:15:58,199
First I need a shelf.

472
00:15:58,199 --> 00:16:00,079
[GIGGLING]

473
00:16:00,079 --> 00:16:01,680
Here's a green shelf.

474
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:03,000
Thank you, Peppa.

475
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,719
Now I need four legs.

476
00:16:05,719 --> 00:16:07,280
[BOTH GIGGLING]

477
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:10,439
One, two, three, four.

478
00:16:10,439 --> 00:16:12,680
Four blue legs, Mummy.

479
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:15,439
Lovely. We'll have this done
in no time.

480
00:16:15,439 --> 00:16:17,439
Here's a red door,
Mummy Pig.

481
00:16:17,439 --> 00:16:19,120
Thank you, Daddy Pig.

482
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:21,599
There. Finished.

483
00:16:21,599 --> 00:16:24,120
Well done, Mummy Pig.

484
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,040
It's very tiny.

485
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:29,400
How will all our toys
fit inside?

486
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:31,199
It is a little small.

487
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:32,319
[SNORTING]

488
00:16:32,319 --> 00:16:34,839
Oh.
George has found another bit.

489
00:16:34,839 --> 00:16:38,040
Uh...
Maybe that's a spare shelf.

490
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,760
And there's
all these bits too.

491
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:42,959
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear, the cupboard is tiny

492
00:16:42,959 --> 00:16:45,839
because Mummy Pig
has not used all the pieces.

493
00:16:45,839 --> 00:16:49,000
We'll just have to take it apart
and start again.

494
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,040
Oh, no.

495
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:53,479
If only we had
the instructions.

496
00:16:53,479 --> 00:16:55,000
[DOORBELL RINGS]

497
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,120
Who can that be?

498
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:00,400
Hello.
I've just found this in my van.

499
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:03,040
It's the missing
instructions.

500
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,879
That will make things
a lot easier.

501
00:17:04,879 --> 00:17:05,800
Hooray!

502
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:07,639
[SNORTING]
[GROANS]

503
00:17:07,639 --> 00:17:10,680
NARRATOR:
The instructions look
very complicated.

504
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,159
It's no good.

505
00:17:12,159 --> 00:17:13,720
It's nonsense.

506
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:15,960
Leave it to me, Daddy Pig.

507
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:18,639
I quite enjoy
putting these things together.

508
00:17:18,639 --> 00:17:19,720
Really?

509
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,720
[SNORTS]
Can we help in any way?

510
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:23,280
You can put the kettle on.

511
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:27,560
I'll have a nice cup of tea
with six sugars, please.

512
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:29,280
[♪♪♪]

513
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,639
NARRATOR:
Everyone is preparing tea
and biscuits

514
00:17:31,639 --> 00:17:32,639
for Mr. Zebra.

515
00:17:32,639 --> 00:17:35,399
Teatime, Mr. Zebra.

516
00:17:35,399 --> 00:17:37,280
Wow!

517
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:40,159
NARRATOR:
Mr. Zebra has built
the toy cupboard.

518
00:17:40,159 --> 00:17:41,760
My goodness, that was quick.

519
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:45,560
Yes, and I've put all your toys
in there too.

520
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:46,840
BOTH:
Ooh.

521
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:48,600
[SNORTS]
Thank you, Mr. Zebra.

522
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:49,560
[SNORTING]

523
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,800
But there's no room

524
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:52,040
for these last two.

525
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:55,280
Oh. Poor Teddy
and Mr. Dinosaur.

526
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,320
Where are they
going to live?

527
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:01,040
Why not simply order another
easy-to-make cupboard?

528
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,240
No!

529
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:04,240
I've got a better idea.

530
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:07,919
Teddy and Mr. Dinosaur
can live on your beds.

531
00:18:07,919 --> 00:18:12,120
But, Mummy,
that's where they lived before.

532
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:13,399
Yes, I know.

533
